to reach the region hit hardest by the  earthquake you need to travel through  some of afghanistan's most challenging  terrain  a week on this long and arduous route is  still the only way much needed help can  get to this disrupted landscape  in this village in burmal district more  than 50 people were killed entire  families wiped out  muhammad roshan lost 18 members of his  family he wants the world to see what  little is left of his home  and  so far muhammad's managed to bury 17 of  his relatives  he's convinced one more body is still  trapped in the rubble  yeah  but  inside his new home a tent with the most  basic facilities lies his sister with a  broken leg it's a rarity women in these  tribal villages are allowed to speak out  but covering her face bibi hawa wants us  to know how she still hasn't had a visit  from a doctor  i'm in pain i can't walk she tells us  all but a few homes in this village have  been flattened the water supply cut off  lost six people from his family he like  everyone else is calling for help to  rebuild his home  seven-year-old mohammed has badly  damaged his leg and with the doctor here  for just a short time he needs treatment  the pain will eventually ease but the  grief of losing the rest of his family  will live with this boy forever  in the neighboring village of lawara  there is more stable continued support  international aid agencies have managed  to set up bases to assist those who've  lost everything  dr tafik was one of the first responders  on the ground  so we are taking patients with trauma so  we receive different type of trauma  fractures and  infected ones  the destruction in this district is  unimaginable and the problem now many  villages face are aftershocks and  landslides  over a week on from one of afghanistan's  deadliest earthquakes and this medical  hub is treating over a hundred people a  day they don't know how long they're  going to be here for  someday though the aid agencies will  pull out but leaving is not an option  for those who survived this earthquake  they face many months perhaps years  literally having to rebuild  their broken lives in zaman rashid sky  news burmal in afghanistan
 

